    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "We are less credulous than we used to be.",
      "translation": "我们现在不像以前那样容易轻信了。",
      "startTime": 13.45,
      "endTime": 17.12,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "credulous",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "轻信的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "In the nineteenth century, a novelist would bring his story to a conclusion by presenting his readers with a series of coincidences--most of them wildly improbable.",
      "translation": "在19世纪，小说家往往通过向读者提供一系列巧合来结束他的故事——其中大多数都是极不可能发生的。",
      "startTime": 17.13,
      "endTime": 30.28,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "improbable",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "不大可能的"
          },
          {
            "word": "coincidence",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "巧合"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Readers happily accepted the fact that an obscure maidservant was really the hero's mother.",
      "translation": "读者竟然愉快地接受了这样一个事实：一个卑微的女佣人竟然是男主人公的生母。",
      "startTime": 30.29,
      "endTime": 37.77,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "obscure",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "不起眼的，卑微的"
          },
          {
            "word": "maidservant",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "女佣"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "A long-lost brother, who was presumed dead, was really alive all the time and wickedly plotting to bring about the hero's downfall. And so on.",
      "translation": "一个失散多年、被认为已经死去的兄弟实际上一直活着，并正阴险地策划着让男主人公败落。如此等等。",
      "startTime": 37.78,
      "endTime": 50.01,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "long-lost",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "失散多年的"
          },
          {
            "word": "presumed",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "推测，假设"
          },
          {
            "word": "downfall",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "衰落，垮台"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Modern readers would find such naive solutions totally unacceptable.",
      "translation": "现代读者会发现这类天真的解决办法完全无法接受。",
      "startTime": 50.02,
      "endTime": 56.12,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "naive",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "天真的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Yet, in real life, circumstances do sometimes conspire to bring about coincidences which anyone but a nineteenth century novelist would find incredible.",
      "translation": "然而在现实生活中，情况有时确实会凑巧，以致产生出除了19世纪小说家外，谁都会觉得难以置信的巧合。",
      "startTime": 56.13,
      "endTime": 69.38,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "conspire",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "阴谋，协力促成"
          },
          {
            "word": "incredible",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "不可思议的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "When I was a boy, my grandfather told me how a German taxi driver, Franz Bussman, found a brother who was thought to have been killed twenty years before.",
